  <bp:ProteinReference rdf:ID="ProteinReference8">
    <bp:organism rdf:resource="#BioSource1" />
    <bp:name rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">UniProt:Q96N66 MBOAT7</bp:name>
    <bp:name rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">MBOAT7</bp:name>
    <bp:name rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">BB1</bp:name>
    <bp:name rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">LENG4</bp:name>
    <bp:name rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">OACT7</bp:name>
    <bp:xref rdf:resource="#UnificationXref62" />
    <bp:comment rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">FUNCTION Acyltransferase which catalyzes the transfer of an acyl group from an acyl-CoA to a lysophosphatidylinositol (1-acylglycerophosphatidylinositol or LPI) leading to the production of a phosphatidylinositol (1,2-diacyl-sn-glycero-3-phosphoinositol or PI) and participates in the reacylation step of the phospholipid remodeling pathway also known as the Lands cycle (PubMed:18094042, PubMed:18772128). Prefers arachidonoyl-CoA as the acyl donor, thus contributing to the regulation of free levels arachidonic acid in cell (PubMed:18094042, PubMed:18772128). In liver, participates in the regulation of triglyceride metabolism through the phosphatidylinositol acyl-chain remodeling regulation (PubMed:32253259).CATALYTIC ACTIVITY a 1-acyl-sn-glycero-3-phospho-(1D-myo-inositol) + (5Z,8Z,11Z,14Z)-eicosatetraenoyl-CoA = a 1-acyl-2-(5Z,8Z,11Z,14Z-eicosatetraenoyl)-sn-glycero-3-phospho-(1D-myo-inositol) + CoACATALYTIC ACTIVITY (5Z,8Z,11Z,14Z)-eicosatetraenoyl-CoA + 1-hexadecanoyl-sn-glycero-3-phosphocholine = 1-hexadecanoyl-2-(5Z,8Z,11Z,14Z-eicosatetraenoyl)-sn-glycero-3-phosphocholine + CoACATALYTIC ACTIVITY a 1-acyl-sn-glycero-3-phospho-(1D-myo-inositol) + an acyl-CoA = a 1,2-diacyl-sn-glycero-3-phospho-(1D-myo-inositol) + CoACATALYTIC ACTIVITY 1-octadecanoyl-sn-glycero-3-phospho-(1D-myo-inositol) + (5Z,8Z,11Z,14Z)-eicosatetraenoyl-CoA = 1-octadecanoyl-2-(5Z,8Z,11Z,14Z-eicosatetraenoyl)-sn-glycero-3-phospho-(1D-myo-inositol) + CoAACTIVITY REGULATION Activity is inhibited by thimerosal.PATHWAY Lipid metabolism; phospholipid metabolism.SUBUNIT Interacts with SPTSSA; the interaction facilitates MBOAT7 location to mitochondria-associated membranes (MAMs).INTERACTION Localized in specific membrane structures termed mitochondria-associated membranes (MAMs) which connect the endoplasmic reticulum (ER) and the mitochondria.ALTERNATIVE PRODUCTS Overexpressed in metastatic breast and bladder carcinomas relative to normal breast epithelium and urothelium.DISEASE The disease is caused by variants affecting the gene represented in this entry.SIMILARITY Belongs to the membrane-bound acyltransferase family.</bp:comment>
  </bp:ProteinReference>
